        '#### Symptom-Titration Rule for SSTAE',
        '   - Within session: if symptoms rise >2–3 points above baseline or the patient\'s pre-session rating during exercise, reduce workload to the previous level immediately. If symptoms do not settle within 5 minutes of reducing workload, end the session.',
        '   - If symptoms have not returned to pre-session baseline within 30 minutes post-exercise, the session dose was too high — reduce target HR or duration at the next session.',
        '   - Next-morning rule: if the patient reports worse symptoms than at baseline on the morning after a session, drop intensity by 5–10 bpm or duration by 5–10 minutes at the next session.',
        '   - The HRt RISES progressively as the underlying physiology recovers — this is the measurable sign of improvement. Retest every 2–3 weeks.',
        '#### The Mechanism of Benefit — Revisited',
        'Each SSTAE session provides a controlled autonomic loading stimulus. The impaired BRS and blunted cerebrovascular CO₂ reactivity are TRAINABLE physiological parameters. Repeated loading just below HRt drives adaptive remodelling: BRS increases, HRV (particularly high-frequency HRV, reflecting vagal tone) normalises, and cerebrovascular CO₂ reactivity approaches pre-injury levels. The HRt rises as these parameters recover — the observable, measurable sign that the physiology is improving. This is the mechanism that justifies daily exercise at a precise, individualised intensity rather than rest.',
