        '#### Neurobiological Mechanisms',
        'Post-concussion anxiety, depression and emotional lability have clear neurobiological underpinnings — they are not simply psychological reactions to injury, though psychological factors amplify them.',
        '   - LIMBIC DYSREGULATION: the amygdala processes emotional salience (fear, threat detection) and is normally regulated by inhibitory input from the medial prefrontal cortex (mPFC). Concussion-related axonal injury to the mPFC-amygdala white matter tracts reduces prefrontal inhibitory control → AMYGDALA HYPERREACTIVITY: heightened emotional responses to non-threatening stimuli, irritability, anxiety and emotional lability.',
